I implemented only the state work. Both operations requests need authority this node doesn't have. The `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, so there is no filesystem or logging interface for `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. There is also no `http-client` interface for the metadata service. Adding either would mean importing a capability outside the node's grant, so I left both out. If operations needs them, the graph would have to grant the node those capabilities. The output is unaffected.

The node marks each considered id as seen, but only when the digest was published. An unpublished digest records nothing, so those items can be retried on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                state_rw::put(id, "1");
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

